{"v":1,"accession":"PRJNA852425","title":"Characterisation of the RNA virome of nine Ochlerotatus species in Finland","description":"RNA viromes of nine commonly encountered Ochlerotatus mosquito species collected around Finland in 2015 and 2017 were studied using next generation sequencing. Mosquito homogenates were sequenced from 91 pools comprising 16-60 morphologically identified adult females of Oc. cantans, Oc. caspius, Oc. communis, Oc. diantaeus, Oc. excrucians, Oc. hexodontus, Oc. intrudens, Oc. pullatus and Oc. punctor/punctodes. In total 514 viral RdRp polymerase sequences of 159 virus species were recovered, belonging to 25 families or equivalent rank, as follows: Aliusviridae, Aspiviridae, Botybirnavirus, Chrysoviridae, Chuviridae, Endornaviridae, Flaviviridae, Iflaviridae, Negevirus, Partitiviridae, Permutotetraviridae, Phasmaviridae, Phenuiviridae, Picornaviridae, Qinviridae, Quenyavirus, Rhabdoviridae, Sedoreoviridae, Solemoviridae, Spinareoviridae, Togaviridae, Totiviridae, Virgaviridae, Xinmoviridae and Yueviridae. Of these 147 are tentatively novel viruses. One sequence of Sindbis virus, which causes Pogosta disease in humans, was detected from Oc. communis from Pohjois-Karjala. This study greatly increases the number of mosquito-associated viruses known from Finland and presents the northern-most mosquito-associated viruses in Europe to date.","center":"University of Helsinki","data_type":"Genome sequencing","submission_date":"2022/06/24 00:00","sample_cols":["accession","title","tier","context","collection_date","collection_year","country","region","place_id","place","location_status","lat","lon","submitted_location","isolation_source","env_broad_scale","env_local_scale","env_medium","eligibility_reason"],"samples":[["SAMN29328841","MIMAG Metagenome-assembled Genome sample from Ochlerotatus punctodes","non_environmental",null,"2015-08-23",2015,"FI","North Ostrobothnia",649924,"Kuusamo","verified",65.6855,29.1345,"Finland: Pohjois-Pohjanmaa, Kuusamo","Whole mosquitoes","Taiga/ Boreal forest","Mixed Coniferous & Deciduous Woodland/ Scrub/ Roadside",null,"host-derived or clinical material"],["SAMN29328844","MIMAG Metagenome-assembled Genome sample from Ochlerotatus excrucians","non_environmental",null,"2015-07-22",2015,"FI",null,null,null,"ambiguous",69.0,27.0,"Finland: Lappi, Inari","Whole mosquitoes","Taiga/ Boreal forest","Fell/ Scrub/ Roadside/ Village",null,"host-derived or clinical material"],["SAMN29328853","MIMAG Metagenome-assembled Genome sample from Ochlerotatus diantaeus","non_environmental",null,"2015-07-23",2015,"FI",null,null,null,"ambiguous",69.0,29.0,"Finland: Lappi, Inari","Whole mosquitoes","Taiga/ Boreal forest","Fell/ Scrub/ Roadside/ Village",null,"host-derived or clinical material"],["SAMN29328854","MIMAG Metagenome-assembled Genome sample from Ochlerotatus diantaeus","non_environmental",null,"2015-07-03",2015,"FI","North Ostrobothnia",652858,"Kiiminki","verified",65.1798,25.8002,"Finland: Pohjois-Pohjanmaa, Kiiminki","Whole mosquitoes","Taiga/ Boreal forest","Mixed Coniferous & Deciduous Woodland/ Roadside",null,"host-derived or clinical material"],["SAMN29328855","MIMAG Metagenome-assembled Genome sample from Ochlerotatus communis","non_environmental",null,"2015-06-26",2015,"FI","North Karelia",656709,"Ilomantsi","verified",62.7666,31.1629,"Finland: Pohjois-Karjala, Ilomantsi","Whole mosquitoes","Taiga/ Boreal forest","Mixed Coniferous & Deciduous Woodland/ Roadside",null,"host-derived or clinical material"],["SAMN29328856","MIMAG Metagenome-assembled Genome sample from Ochlerotatus pullatus","non_environmental",null,"2015-07-02",2015,"FI","Satakunta",648886,"Lappi","verified",null,null,"Finland: Lappi","Whole mosquitoes","Taiga/ Boreal forest","Roadside/ Scrub",null,"host-derived or clinical material"],["SAMN29328857","MIMAG Metagenome-assembled Genome sample from Ochlerotatus communis","non_environmental",null,"2015-07-19",2015,"FI",null,null,null,"ambiguous",66.0,28.0,"Finland: Lap